  "rootCause": "ANALYSIS_MISSING_SIGNAL",
  "rootCauseEvidence": "two findings on one run. (1) DEPLOY-005 third shape: memos reads MEMOS_DSN through viper's env prefix (viper.SetEnvPrefix('memos') + GetString('dsn')), a name that appears nowhere as a literal, so the env-var model held one variable and no url alias was bound; with the vendor's MEMOS_DRIVER=postgres the configured revision dialled its default 127.0.0.1:5432 and exited four times (fix PR #226, analysis v18). (2) DEPLOY-015: ECS's circuit breaker rolled the service back to the unconfigured template revision, which runs the same pinned image and booted on SQLite; the relay's success gate held on it and DEPLOY_RELEASE was reported SUCCEEDED (alreadyRunning) with the deployment HEALTHY over default HTTPS — a false success the harness caught only through the observation window's crash count (fix PR #225, relay). Cleanup: Disconnect and Purge through the product; connector removal and leak audit first failed on the expired aws login, then passed on the cleanup rerun.",
